<title>NETHERLANDS: FORECAST - Dutch May CPI seen rising 1.9 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>FORECAST - Dutch May CPI seen rising 1.9 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-06-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dutch economists expect Dutch May consumer price inflation to show a 1.9 percent rise year-on-year, compared with a year-on-year rise of 1.8 percent in April.</p>
<p>Rabo pointed to a sharp rise in coffee prices in May, which is likely to be partially offset by lower prices of fruits and vegetables. The data will be released on Friday at 0830 GMT.</p>
<p>Economists' forecasts are summarised below:</p>
<p>GMT---Date--Period--Indicator-------Consensus---Range----Pvs</p>
<p> 0830  6/6   May     CPI Mth/Mth     0.0 pct   -0.1/0.0   0.0</p>
<p> 0830  6/6   May     CPI Yr/Yr	 1.9 pct    1.7/2.0   1.8</p>
<p>Forecasts contributed by: ABN AMRO, Generale Bank, ING, MeesPierson, NIB Securities, Rabobank.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
